      "problem": "Find an expression for the volume $V$ of a cylinder in terms of $h$ given that $\\frac{r}{h}=\\frac{1}{2},$ where $r$ is the radius of the base and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.",
      "worked_solution": "Our goal is to express $V$ in terms of $h.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $r$ in the above equation, which we do using cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2r & =h \\\\ r & =\\frac{h}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $r=\\frac{h}{2}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\pi {(\\frac{h}{2})}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot \\frac{{h}^{2}}{4}\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi {h}^{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
