      "dom_id": "question-117876",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate the height $h$ of a cylinder given that its volume is $72\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{3}$ and the ratio of its radius to its height is $3.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that  the ratio of the radius of the base $r$ to the height $h$ is $3,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =3 \\\\ r & =3h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V=72\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{3}$ and $r=3h$ into the formula, we find the value of $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 72\\pi  & =\\pi {(3h)}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\ 72 & =9{h}^{3} \\\\ {h}^{3} & =8 \\\\ h & =2\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
